<<~ ahu slot=`#/2-law-x-domain-matrix`>>

!! 2. Law x domain matrix

Legend: ON = serves it; opt = serves where a carrier opts in by tag; NEVER = must not touch (fiction voice or record); fmt = carrier-format floor, not intent.

Laws: (a) status-why + closed 5-stage vocabulary; (b) canon-history / dated-history; (c) retired words (s-vocabulary); (d) quoted `lar:` positional; (e) carrier shape (DOCTYPE, type, one body, fence spelling, `$` name); (f) dangling edges / empty room; (g) existing check: frame/bcc re-stamp, duplicate key, torn frame; (h) existing: stage-owes (open lean / fold target).

| law | lares api | lares docs | lararium api/mesh/browser | lararium docs | crossroads/ref/library | elyncia (+referee) | sdm | daemon / working memory |h
| (a) status-why + vocab | opt | opt (home turf: designs/handoffs) | opt | opt | skip | opt (see 3) | opt | NEVER (stage not yet a doc; scratch) |
| (b) canon-history | ON | NEVER (records narrate history by design) | ON | NEVER | ref/library NEVER (quoted) | NEVER | NEVER (LEAN) | NEVER |
| (c) retired words | ON | ON (LEAN: the word retires house-wide in prose) | ON | ON | ref/library NEVER | NEVER (a fiction name may collide) | NEVER (LEAN) | NEVER |
| (d) quoted positional | ON | ON | ON | ON | ON where sigils appear | ON where sigils appear (grammar fault, not voice) | ON | ON |
| (e) shape | fmt | fmt | fmt | fmt | fmt | fmt | fmt | fmt |
| (f) dangling edges | ON (staged only) | ON (staged) | ON (staged) | ON (staged) | n/a | LEAN opt (loulou edges are rare; books index) | opt | n/a |
| (g) frame/bcc, dup key, torn | fmt | fmt | fmt | fmt | fmt | fmt | fmt | fmt |
| (h) stage-owes | opt, rides (a) | opt | opt | opt | skip | opt | opt | NEVER |

Rulings behind the cells:
* (a) opt: otakiage THE RULING, 2026-09-12: "A carrier carrying no lifecycle/* tag stands UNGOVERNED... `meme check` enforces nothing new on it"; "A missing tag MUST NOT read as a stage". RULED. Today 63 of ~800 carriers carry a lifecycle tag (40 lares, 23 lararium, none elsewhere). The scout's proposal to make "stage without status-why" a check error needs no scoping: it already reads only tagged carriers. Moving it into `meme check` is consistent with the ruling; the operator's note is already honoured by the tag.
* (b) path scope: evergreen-boundary `isCanonFile` = `bags/*/*/*/(api|mesh|browser)/**.mem`, never `docs/` (RULED in evergreen-sweep-2026 G37; code comment line 249). Path-scoped already; elyncia's `concepts/` etc. never match because the path lacks api|mesh|browser. So (b) never touches fiction today. NEVER cells hold by construction.
* (c) the scout's "canon half" runs over canon prose; scope = same path class as (b) unless the operator wants docs too. LEAN.
* (d)(e)(g) are grammar and format: a broken sigil or missing frame fails to load or parse in ANY wiki, so they follow the carrier, not the intent. LEAN: stay universal (they exist or are cheap), but each `meme check` rule must still be a distinct function the domain gate can mute.
* Fiction fence: rpg-materials ruling, "in-world narration keeps its own voice". RULED for chapters; LEAN that it extends to the elyncia bag carriers.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/3-o-takiage-per-domain`>>

!! 3. o-takiage per domain (lean only)

Read whole: otakiage.mem (478 lines). Five stages designed, standing, folded, harvest, retiring (plus fleeting/gone as no-carrier states), tag family, `kind/rite` beside, `status-why` witness sentence, fire is CALLED never scheduled, kapu/tombstone siblings outside the fire. Its table already lists "a fiction-canon concept" among carriers that enter no lifecycle; #/questions asks whether any class MUST carry one (still open).

''RPG chapters'' (`elyncia/ ftls/ sdm/ wtf/` md roots now; `bags/elyncia`, `bags/sdm` carriers later). Intent: players and GMs read the chapters; the work is an evolving book. The software ladder does not map; the book's own ladder is draft -> playtested -> print-ready -> errata'd -> superseded.
* LEAN: do NOT reuse the five stage words. A chapter is neither "standing = ruling enacted" nor "folded = pointers alone". Use a second tag family `edition/*` only if the operator wants it: `edition/draft`, `edition/playtest`, `edition/table-ready`, `edition/superseded`. `superseded` plays "retiring": the chapter keeps its address (the old name must keep meaning what it meant, meme#/retirement) and points forward to the new edition; nothing burns while a table plays from it.
* `status-why` fit: LEAN weak. For a chapter the witness sentence would read "run at table X on date" (a playtest note), a real witness, but optional. Keep it free, not gated.
* "folded" for an RPG chapter: content moved into another chapter (e.g. the Style Base Layer folded into the Referee Guide). Pointers-alone is legal, and the rpg ruling already holds back "Style Base Layer and Referee Guide drafts" &#45;- a natural first use.
* The fire: never fires on published chapters; third-party rights (Thracia maps, OSR PDFs, Caverns) make `_osr/source-pdfs` a kapu-like "never burns" class.
* Until the lararium stands the md roots carry no tags at all; the migration (MD &lt;-> memetic-wikitext reprojection) is ruled to wait. So today this is a design, not a gate.

''Concept art'' (inside bags/elyncia as character packages; rating `ano`). Intent: a sheet is a render brief plus its outcome: palette, directions, negative directions, prompt. Its life: prompt drafted -> rendered -> chosen -> locked as canon visual -> superseded by a re-render.
* LEAN: a tag family `art/*`: `art/brief`, `art/rendered`, `art/locked`, `art/superseded`. `locked` is the only stage with teeth: other carriers cite its palette and the art-sigil spec (`api/art-sigils/spec.mem`) governs the prompt grammar.
* "retiring" for a sheet: a superseded render stays as a record of why the palette moved; the old prompt is harvest material for the next sheet (harvest to the living sheet, not to nothing). Never burns while any locked sheet cites it by `loulou`.
* `status-why` fit: GOOD where it names the render evidence (image CID, MidJourney job, date) &#45;- the witness sentence maps directly onto "which render proves this locked".
* Where it lives: no art wiki or bag exists. LEAN: do not mint one; art stays under the character it serves (the existing arrangement). A separate art domain would add a registry row nobody asked for.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/4-declaring-a-domain-options-least-new-shape`>>

!! 4. Declaring a domain: options, least new shape

| option | what exists today | new shape | verdict |h
| carrier's own tag | `lifecycle/*` tag already switches laws (a)(h) per carrier; `kind/rite` beside it; ruled | none | BEST for intent-driven laws |
| path class | `isCanonFile` already scopes (b) to `api|mesh|browser`, never `docs/` or other bags; RULED G37 | none | BEST for canon-register laws (b)(c) |
| bag `meta.mem` key | every bag meta already carries `bag`, `cap-tier`, `home`, `repository` (6 bags) | one key, e.g. `laws = [...]` or `intent = "fiction"` | the one new key, only if a law must differ per bag and path/tag cannot say it |
| recipe field | wiki-recipe.ts carries slots and library bags, no intent field | a schema change plus fingerprint churn | REJECT (recipes compose layers; intent is not composition; also bags are canon, wikis are composition) |
| namespace | `uri-path` roots by bag already (`ha.ka.ba/elyncia/...`) | none | falls out of path class |

Recommendation: no new declaration. Each law names its reach by the mark it already reads: (a)(h) by tag, (b)(c) by path class, (d)(e)(g) universal by format. Add the bag `meta.mem` key only when a law needs "this whole bag" and `isCanonFile`-style path matching proves too blunt (probably the day an elyncia law arrives, such as an `edition/*` family). Test shape: each moved law gains a CONTROL (an ungoverned/fiction carrier stays exit 0), as the otakiage control already does.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/5-forks-talked-out`>>

!! 5. Forks talked out (two rounds)

# Should the format floor (DOCTYPE, type) be switchable per domain? Round 1: operator says not every meme enforces all laws. Round 2: DOCTYPE and `type` decide whether the engine loads a carrier at all, and every elyncia carrier already carries both; switching them off helps no domain. SURVIVES NOT. Stays universal. (Operator may overrule.)
# Does (b) canon-history need a domain declaration? Round 1: yes, fiction. Round 2: the path class already excludes everything but api/mesh/browser. DIES.
# Mint an art wiki/bag and an RPG wiki now? Round 2: the ruling holds migration until the lararium stands. DIES, until founding.
# Should dangling-edge refusal reach fiction? Round 2: staged-only refusal would block an author adding a `[[...]]`-style link to a not-yet-written chapter, which is the normal drafting motion in fiction. SURVIVES as ask.
# Does retired-word (c) reach `docs/`? Round 1 yes, Round 2 the scout's rows name only canon prose ("no retired key abbreviation in canon prose"). Lean canon-only; SURVIVES as a small ask.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/6-operator-asks`>>

!! 6. Operator asks (each with lean)

# Edge refusal on staged carriers: apply to fiction (elyncia, sdm) or only lares/lararium? LEAN: lares and lararium only; fiction drafts freely.
# Retired words (s-vocabulary): canon path only (api/mesh/browser), or docs too? LEAN: canon only, matching the scout.
# May RPG chapters and art sheets get their own tag families (`edition/*`, `art/*`) when the lararium stands, rather than the five software stages? LEAN: yes, and not before; record in the otakiage #/questions slot "does any class MUST carry one" as answered "no, by domain".
# Which bags are operator-only fiction (elyncia, elyncia-referee, sdm) so a fence can read it? No canon states it; the fence rests in memory (rpg ruling) and not in CLAUDE.md. LEAN: say it once in the bag's own `meta.mem` prose, no new key.

